IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nz-part2-principles`

-- Tests for nz-part2-principles.l4 (ss 8 to 12).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.

§ `Section 9 -- Application of this Part`

-- src:93 | 9 Application of this Part
-- src:94 | A provision of this Part applies to legislation that is part of the laws of New Zealand unless—
-- src:95 | the legislation provides otherwise; or
-- src:96 | the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation.
-- src:97 | The provisions of this Part also apply to the interpretation of this Act.
-- (1) applies to legislation that is part of the laws of New Zealand unless the legislation provides otherwise or the context requires a different interpretation.
-- Arguments: part of the laws of New Zealand, provides otherwise, context requires a different interpretation.
#ASSERT `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- (2) The provisions of this Part also apply to the interpretation of this Act.
#ASSERT `Part 2 is applied to the interpretation of` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Part 2 is applied to the interpretation of` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 10 -- How to ascertain meaning of legislation`

-- src:99 | 10 How to ascertain meaning of legislation
-- src:100 | The meaning of legislation must be ascertained from its text and in the light of its purpose and its context.
-- src:101 | Subsection (1) applies whether or not the legislation’s purpose is stated in the legislation.
-- src:102 | The text of legislation includes the indications provided in the legislation.
-- src:103 | Examples of those indications are preambles, a table of contents, headings, diagrams, graphics, examples and explanatory material, and the organisation and format of the legislation.
-- (1) text, purpose and context: all three.
#ASSERT `the meaning of legislation must be ascertained from` `the text of the legislation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the meaning of legislation must be ascertained from` `the purpose of the legislation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the meaning of legislation must be ascertained from` `the context of the legislation` EQUALS TRUE

-- (2) whether or not the purpose is stated in the legislation.
#ASSERT `the purpose is used to ascertain the meaning` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the purpose is used to ascertain the meaning` FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- (3) and (4) the text includes the indications provided in the legislation; each listed example is text when provided, none is when not provided.
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `a preamble` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `a table of contents` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `a heading` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `a diagram` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `a graphic` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `an example` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `explanatory material` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `the organisation and format of the legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `the organisation of the legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `the format of the legislation` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `another indication` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `a heading` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an indication is part of the text of the legislation` `another indication` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 11 -- Legislation applies to circumstances as they arise`

-- src:104 | 11 Legislation applies to circumstances as they arise
-- src:105 | Legislation applies to circumstances as they arise.
-- In force from the day it comes into force (s 27: at the start of that day), no repeal day: a circumstance on the first day, or after, is governed; the day before is not.
#ASSERT `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` (Date 1 1 2030) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE

-- With a repeal day (s 39: repealed at the start of that day): the day before the repeal day is governed; the repeal day itself is not.
#ASSERT `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` (Date 31 5 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` (Date 2 6 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 12 -- Legislation does not have retrospective effect`

-- src:106 | 12 Legislation does not have retrospective effect
-- src:107 | Legislation does not have retrospective effect.
-- A circumstance that arose before the legislation came into force is not governed by it; one on the first day, or after, is.
#ASSERT `whether the legislation applies to a circumstance that arose on` (Date 28 2 2026) `when it came into force on` (Date 1 3 2026) `and it provides otherwise` FALSE EQUALS `The legislation does not apply: no retrospective effect`
#ASSERT `whether the legislation applies to a circumstance that arose on` (Date 1 3 2026) `when it came into force on` (Date 1 3 2026) `and it provides otherwise` FALSE EQUALS `The legislation applies`
#ASSERT `whether the legislation applies to a circumstance that arose on` (Date 2 3 2026) `when it came into force on` (Date 1 3 2026) `and it provides otherwise` FALSE EQUALS `The legislation applies`
-- s 9(1)(a): where the legislation provides otherwise, s 12 gives way (fork F7).
#ASSERT `whether the legislation applies to a circumstance that arose on` (Date 28 2 2026) `when it came into force on` (Date 1 3 2026) `and it provides otherwise` TRUE EQUALS `The legislation applies`
